# What `docker build -f projects/builder/Dockerfile .` leaves out of the
# context (AGAST #4822).  BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the
# Dockerfile, so this one file applies to the builder image only; a
# .dockerignore at the repository root would apply to every image built from
# it.
#
# test.sh builds from `git archive <commit>`, which is already clean.  This
# is for a build from a working tree: it must see the same tree, so a stale
# build product cannot stand in for the bootstrap, and nothing private gets
# into a layer.

# Version control and editor state.
.git
**/.git
.claude
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Build products and caches.  A working tree's ritz1/build/ritz1 would make
# `make ritz1-bootstrap` skip stage 1; the image must build it from source.
**/build
**/.ritz-cache*
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.o
**/*.ll.tmp

# Secrets and local configuration.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.docker
**/.netrc
